        "tag": "v0.4.1",
        "body": "## Install (no npm account needed)\n\n```bash\nnpm install github:auroraxo/sememe#v0.4.1\n```\n\n```js\nimport { decodePayload } from 'sememe';\n```\n\nThe registry name is deliberately unpublished (no name squatting): the git tag is the release artifact.\n\n## What's in v0.4.1\n\n- **The README's peer-refusal claim is now true.** It said the CLI \"refuses `sememe pull` without [the optional peer] ... and still runs every other subcommand\" — but `sememe gap` probes the same on-chain IDL addresses, so it needs the peer too and refuses as well. Measured on the installed tree (2026-11-05): 2 of 13 subcommands need `@solana/web3.js` (`gap`, `pull`), the README named 1.\n- `tools/measure-release-surface.mjs` now derives the peer-needing commands statically from the bin's import graph and fails the README when the claim and the tree disagree.\n- The install pins point at `v0.4.1`, whose tree ships everything the README documents (`sememe gap`, `sememe/raydium`, `sememe/token-metadata`).\n\n## Honest limits\n\nNo external users yet (0 non-owner signals), not an audit, own-host measurement. Instruction-data decoding is the proven path; account/event decoding is exercised by tests but not by an outside consumer. `sememe gap` and `sememe pull` need `@solana/web3.js`; every other subcommand runs without it.\n",
        "draft": false,
        "prerelease": false,
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-05T06:14:11Z",
        "createdAt": "2026-11-05T06:14:08Z"
      },
      {
        "tag": "v0.4.0",
        "body": "## Install (no npm account needed)\n\n```bash\nnpm install github:auroraxo/sememe#v0.4.0\n```\n\n```js\nimport { decodePayload } from 'sememe';\n```\n\nThe registry name is deliberately unpublished (no name squatting): the git tag is the release artifact. This release exists because `releases/` used to be empty while the README pinned `#v0.3.0` — a tree that shipped neither `sememe gap` nor `sememe/raydium`.\n\n## What's in v0.4.0\n\n- `sememe gap <program>` — classify one program's acquisition gap (pullable / no-interface-published / present-undecodable / vendored / unknown; RPC failure exits 3, never a fake absence).\n- `sememe/raydium` export subpath and `decode-raydium` / `raydium-provenance` commands.\n- Release-surface measurement: `tools/measure-release-surface.mjs` derives the pre-fix verdict defect-by-defect from committed inputs (`research/release-surface-2026-11-05-before.json`).\n\n## Honest limits\n\nNo external users yet (0 non-owner signals), not an audit, own-host measurement; instruction-data decoding is the proven path, account/event decoding is exercised by tests but not by an outside consumer.\n",
